    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2003192750133613030",
      "url": "https://x.com/DrTonyLeachon/status/2003192750133613030",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/DrTonyLeachon/status/2003192750133613030",
      "text": "Plunder of PhilHealth: A Betrayal of Universal Health Care\n\nby Dr. Tony Leachon\n\nExecutive Secretary Ralph Recto, together with former PhilHealth president Emmanuel Ledesma, now faces plunder charges before the Ombudsman. \n\nThe complaint filed by the Save the Philippines Coalition exposes the unconstitutional diversion of ₱60 billion in PhilHealth funds—resources meant for healthcare services—into the National Treasury.\n\nThis was not an accident. It was a premeditated act, engineered through a flawed rider provision in the GAA that siphoned PhilHealth’s earmarked resources into unprogrammed appropriations and flood control projects. \n\nThe result: millions of poor and unemployed Filipinos stripped of health coverage, in direct violation of the Universal Health Care Act and the Sin Tax Law.\n\nRecto cannot feign ignorance. His record reveals a consistent pattern:\n\n• He voted against the Sin Tax in 2012, undermining health reforms.\n\n• He authored regressive taxation measures like VAT, burdening ordinary Filipinos.\n\n• He misled the public with claims of a “record-breaking ₱113 billion subsidy” for PhilHealth, when in truth, ₱60 billion was merely restored by Supreme Court order.\n\nThis is technical malversation and plunder. Good faith cannot excuse deliberate defunding. \n\nThe law is clear: PhilHealth funds belong to its members and cannot be diverted without legal basis.\n\nUniversal Health Care is not a slogan—it is a covenant. To defund PhilHealth is to betray justice, dignity, and the right to health.\n\nWe demand:\n\n• Accountability from those who orchestrated this betrayal.\n• Transparency in allocations.\n• Judicial enforcement to protect the UHC Act.\n\nRalph Recto must face the consequences of his actions. \n\nThe fight for PhilHealth funding is the fight for the soul of our healthcare system. Anything less is a betrayal of the nation.\n\n#RelentlessForChange\n#Ombudsman #PhilHealth #UHC #Accountability\n\nTony Leachon",
